T2 WORKLOG: camera backends (Argus primary, GStreamer fallback, mock, replay) + IMX519 focus + ec-cam-probe
=========================================================================================================
State: R1 fixes DONE (F3 F10 F11 F12 F14 F16), awaiting R1 re-verification. Nothing in progress; build trees deleted.

R1 fixes (2026-10-27/28)
- F3: sensor_clock: kMaxFutureCameraStampNs = 2 ms (configurable arg of classify_sensor_clock and
  SensorClockResolver); Argus counts future stamps via CameraBase::count_timestamp_anomaly. Tests added.
- F10: ec-cam-probe --focus-sweep refuses non-real cameras (mock/replay/gst override) and fails (exit 1) when no step
  moved the lens; best position only over effective steps.
- F11: gst test suppressions -> one `called_from_lib:` template per GLib/GStreamer module (TSan aborts if a template
  matches two libraries; a GMutex locked in libglib and unlocked from a plugin must be ignored on both sides).
  Consequence: GLib's pthread_create is ignored, so the start() -> streaming-thread and callback -> stop() edges are
  declared with __tsan_release/__tsan_acquire on GstCamera::tsan_sync_ (TSan builds only); GstCamera also gained a
  real armed_/inflight_ hand-over (no sample is processed while starting/stopping) and reads base time from the
  appsink instead of pipeline_. TSan-only death test GstTsan.InjectedRaceInAppsinkCallbackIsReported proves a race
  in an appsink callback is reported (it was hidden by the old race:libgst* suppressions).
- F12: mock FIFO model: frames more than buffer_count periods late are lost (seq gaps); mock tests use
  buffer_count = 256 for determinism under load; BehindRealTimeDropsBeyondFifo tests the overflow.
  NOTE for T5: mock FIFO depth = driver.buffer_count; use a large value in deterministic tests.
- F14: replay uses rig/package/layout.hpp (kFramesDir, kCamData, kFrameMeta); tests write kFrameMetaHeader.
- F16: CONTRACT CHANGE (additive): types.hpp enum ColorRange {kUnknown, kLimited, kFull} + to_string, and
  FrameMeta::color_range (default kUnknown). Argus: NVBUF_COLOR_FORMAT_NV12_ER (full range) for nv12/gray8, NV12
  (video range) blit for bgr/rgb (OpenCV YUV2BGR_NV12 expects video range) -> kFull. GStreamer: from the caps
  colorimetry (videotestsrc/videoconvert NV12 = kLimited; nvvidconv: checked on H). Mock/replay: JFIF YCbCr via
  COLOR_BGR2YCrCb -> kFull (test: pure red -> Y 76, Cb 85, Cr 255).
- Argus compile-only re-run with NV12_ER (headers re-extracted, same sha256, then deleted): OK.
- Gates (--jobs 4): default PASS 393/393; TSan 394/394 (full ctest; the first check.sh pass had one failure in T3's
  CaptureService.FromRigConfigWithMockBackends from a stale build of T3's concurrently edited test, passed after
  rebuild); ASan+UBSan PASS 393/393, 0 UBSan runtime errors. All trees ($SCRATCH/build/t2fix*) deleted.
- T3's layout rename (kFramesDir = "data") has landed; replay + tests use the constant (T1's earlier
  ReplayTest.PackageFolderWithMetaAndRecordedDrops failure predates that).

