Decisions + contract notes (so far)
- getSensorTimestamp() = "time that the first data from this capture arrives from the sensor"
  (CaptureMetadata.h r36.4.3) = start of readout of row 0 = END of row 0 exposure. The frozen ImageFrame defines
  t_sof_ns as "first row starts exposing", so ArgusCamera sets t_sof_ns = sensor_ts - exposure; then
  mid_exposure_time() gives t_mid = sensor_ts - exposure/2 + readout/2. Using sensor_ts directly as t_sof would
  make t_mid one full exposure late (8 ms main, 4 ms uw). No declaration change.
- getFrameReadoutTime = "from the beginning of the first line to the beginning of the last line" -> +readout/2 for
  the middle row. Cross-check: Ext::ISensorTimestampTsc EOF - SOF.
- Clock domain conflicting (forum 268916: JerryChang says MONOTONIC_RAW, ShaneCCC says CLOCK_REALTIME; TSC SOF minus
  /sys/devices/system/clocksource/clocksource0/offset_ns = MONOTONIC_RAW). Plan: classify at runtime against
  raw/mono/realtime, prefer raw; cross-check with TSC - offset_ns; fail loudly if implausible.
- Mode "full_fov" = no crop relative to the sensor's reference field: IMX219 = full 3280x2464 array; IMX519 = the
  3840x2160 16:9 field (1920x1080 = 2x2 bin of it). IMX519 1280x720 is a 2x2 bin of a 2560x1440 crop -> narrower
  FOV -> full_fov=false (finding: PIPELINE 3's "1920x1080 or 1280x720" choice changes the FOV; capture 1080p).
- fps match needs tolerance: Argus reports 1080p60 as 59.999999 (Duration 16666667).
- VCM is powered with the sensor: focus is written after streaming starts (first frame), else it is lost.
- CONTRACT NOTE (additive): CameraStats gained time_source, tsc_cross_check_ns, timestamp_anomalies, focus_detail
  (defaulted, at the end of the struct). New public headers under rig/drivers/camera/ (T2's own module).
- T3 cross-check: common/config/sensor_modes.cpp marks imx519 1920x1080/3840x2160 full_fov=false; with the frozen
  select_sensor_mode rule that would make the configured main mode unselectable. T2 uses the reference-field
  definition (sensor_modes.hpp). Reviewer: align T3's table (and its 1280x720 = narrower crop).
- Replay: end of data -> status kOutOfRange "end of replay"; images delivered at their stored size.
- frame_meta.csv columns parsed by replay (proposal for T5): t_ns,t_sof_ns,t_arrival_ns,seq,exposure_ns,
  analog_gain,digital_gain,readout_ns,sensor_mode,focus_position,focus_status (header row, any order).
- GstCamera: timed settle (1 s) only with a real nvarguscamerasrc or after a focus write; deferred AE/AWB locks are
  applied by g_object_set at runtime [H: verify nvarguscamerasrc honours a runtime awblock change].
- Focus never fails start(); status recorded per frame and in stats.focus_detail.
- LSan: libglib allocates 16 KiB in a loader-run constructor; gst test + ec-cam-probe define
  __lsan_default_suppressions "leak:ld-linux" + __asan_default_options fast_unwind_on_malloc=0 (precise: only stacks
  through the dynamic loader are suppressed).
- TSan: GLib/GStreamer are uninstrumented (atomics/lock-free GstAtomicQueue invisible) -> module-scoped race
  suppressions in tests/camera/gst/test_gst_camera.cpp only; the rig side of the queued backends is TSan-tested
  without GStreamer in tests/camera/test_camera_base.cpp. Replay test: "deadlock:libgdal.so" (OpenCV imgcodecs loads
  libgdal; single-thread lock-order report inside GDAL).

